1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,100
Last time, we added two numbers on one rod, but one rod can only show up to nine.

2
00:00:08,220 --> 00:00:11,100
So what do we do when a number is bigger than nine?

3
00:00:12,460 --> 00:00:14,160
That's what the other rods are for.

4
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:20,100
On an abacus this size, the ones rod is the one on the far right.

5
00:00:21,040 --> 00:00:25,200
On a much bigger abacus, the ones rod sits in the middle instead.

6
00:00:25,820 --> 00:00:28,060
We saw that in the first video.

7
00:00:29,120 --> 00:00:32,700
Now look at the rod just to the left of the ones rod.

8
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:35,460
That one is the tens rod.

9
00:00:36,460 --> 00:00:40,500
Every bead on the tens rod is worth ten, not one.

10
00:00:41,780 --> 00:00:42,940
Let's make ten.

11
00:00:44,380 --> 00:00:46,980
Push one lower bead up on the tens rod.

12
00:00:48,060 --> 00:00:49,940
Leave the ones rod at zero.

13
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:56,420
One bead on the tens rod is one ten, and one ten is ten.

14
00:00:58,060 --> 00:00:59,740
Now let's make twenty-three.

15
00:01:00,980 --> 00:01:04,320
On the tens rod, push two lower beads up.

16
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:09,580
Two beads on the tens rod is two tens, which is twenty.

17
00:01:10,980 --> 00:01:14,620
Now on the ones rod, push three lower beads up.

18
00:01:15,520 --> 00:01:16,760
That is three ones.

19
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:20,180
Twenty and three is twenty-three.

20
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:24,900
Here's how to read any number on two rods.

21
00:01:26,140 --> 00:01:27,620
Read the tens rod first.

22
00:01:28,480 --> 00:01:30,400
Then read the ones rod.

23
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:33,620
Let's try fifty-six.

24
00:01:35,140 --> 00:01:37,840
On the tens rod, push the upper bead down.

25
00:01:38,880 --> 00:01:43,820
The upper bead on the tens rod is worth five tens, which is fifty.

26
00:01:45,260 --> 00:01:48,660
On the ones rod, push the upper bead down for five.

27
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:52,520
Then push one lower bead up for one.

28
00:01:53,620 --> 00:01:55,200
That makes six ones.

29
00:01:56,560 --> 00:01:58,780
Fifty and six is fifty-six.

30
00:02:00,220 --> 00:02:03,220
What's the biggest number that two rods can show?

31
00:02:04,280 --> 00:02:09,980
On the tens rod, push the upper bead down and all four lower beads up.

32
00:02:11,180 --> 00:02:13,780
That is nine tens, which is ninety.

33
00:02:15,220 --> 00:02:18,140
Now do exactly the same on the ones rod.

34
00:02:19,460 --> 00:02:20,600
That is nine ones.

35
00:02:22,060 --> 00:02:24,260
Ninety and nine is ninety-nine.

36
00:02:25,460 --> 00:02:29,440
Ninety-nine is the biggest number that two rods can show.

37
00:02:30,780 --> 00:02:36,360
So with two rods, you can make every number from zero to ninety-nine.

38
00:02:37,460 --> 00:02:39,700
That's one hundred different numbers.

39
00:02:41,260 --> 00:02:42,820
Now it's your turn.

40
00:02:44,060 --> 00:02:48,220
The tens rod shows three, and the ones rod shows eight.

41
00:02:49,380 --> 00:02:50,500
What number is that?

42
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:54,820
Three tens is thirty.

43
00:02:55,720 --> 00:02:57,720
Eight ones is eight.

44
00:02:58,720 --> 00:03:01,200
Thirty and eight is thirty-eight.

45
00:03:02,300 --> 00:03:03,300
Great job!

46
00:03:04,720 --> 00:03:06,660
And it doesn't stop at two rods.

47
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:10,680
The next rod to the left is the hundreds rod.

48
00:03:11,880 --> 00:03:14,980
Every bead on that rod is worth one hundred.

49
00:03:16,340 --> 00:03:22,800
Two beads on the hundreds rod, four on the tens rod, and seven on the ones rod.

50
00:03:23,600 --> 00:03:26,040
Two hundred, forty-seven.

51
00:03:27,140 --> 00:03:33,060
Every time you move one rod to the left, each bead is worth ten times more.

52
00:03:34,660 --> 00:03:38,200
Now try making some big numbers on your own abacus.

53
00:03:39,060 --> 00:03:43,420
If you enjoyed this video, please like and subscribe for more.

54
00:03:44,600 --> 00:03:48,720
Search for abacus kids on the Apple App Store or Google Play.

55
00:03:49,480 --> 00:03:50,580
Download it free.

56
00:03:51,620 --> 00:03:57,140
See you in the next video where we learn how to take numbers away on the abacus.
